hw/sd/sd: let -device emmc be created from the command line

The eMMC model (TYPE_EMMC) is marked not user-creatable, because an
eMMC is soldered to a board and a machine that has one creates it
itself. None of the RISC-V machines does, so a guest's MMC driver has
nothing to talk to: microchip-icicle-kit has the Cadence SD4HC the
BeagleV-Fire uses for its 16GB eMMC, but only ever an SD card on it.

Making the model user-creatable lets a test put an eMMC on that bus
(-drive if=none,id=e,... -device emmc,drive=e) and exercise the MMC
side of a driver: CMD1, a host-assigned RCA, EXT_CSD's sector count,
the CMD6 bus-width switch. It changes nothing for a machine that does
not ask for one.

--- a/hw/sd/sd.c
+++ b/hw/sd/sd.c
@@ -2876,7 +2876,7 @@
     dc->realize = emmc_realize;
     device_class_set_props(dc, emmc_properties);
     /* Reason: Soldered on board */
-    dc->user_creatable = false;
+    dc->user_creatable = true;
 
     sc->proto = &sd_proto_emmc;
 
